                </g>
            </svg>
            @* Editable "Support and guidance" footer block — heading + contact prose only.
               Managed from the admin content-blocks page.

               The statutory link row that used to live in here has been pulled out into the
               static markup below. An accessibility statement link is a legal requirement
               under the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2)
               Accessibility Regulations 2018, so it must not be something a CMS editor can
               retarget, blank, or leave as a placeholder `#`.

               Note the `-v2` key suffix. `IContentBlockService.EnsureAsync` seeds defaultHtml
               only when no block exists for the key, so editing defaultHtml alone is inert on
               every database that already holds the old block — it would have kept rendering
               the stale `#` links alongside the new static row. A new key seeds cleanly on
               deploy. The old `footer-support-and-guidance` block is left orphaned (visible in
               /admin/content-blocks, no longer rendered) rather than deleted, so any hand-
               edited prose can still be recovered and pasted across. *@
            @await Component.InvokeAsync("EditableContent", new {
                key = "footer-support-and-guidance-v2",
                defaultHtml = @"<h2 class=""govuk-heading-m"">Support and guidance</h2>
<p>If you have a question, or you're having a problem using this service, you can <a href=""/contact"" class=""govuk-link"">send us a message</a> or call us on 0300 131 2762</p>"
            })
            
